ruan SMP diagnostics (xnu-12377). Every secondary-CPU step becomes an [ev] line in the ramoops ring (package/RuanMacBootProgress.c
ruan_smp_event), which is written uncached and survives a hard reset; steps before the MMU is on leave a per-core breadcrumb
(ruan_smp_crumb, one 64-byte line per MPIDR Aff1) that the 1 s heartbeat prints as " c<n>=<step>@<ms>/a<ArmCpu step>":
1 reset_vector, 2 cpu data found, 3 handler ok, 4 start_cpu, 5 common_start (MMU still off), 6 arm_init_cpu (MMU on),
e no cpu data / bad handler, f0+n exception in LowExceptionVectorBase slot n (ESR/ELR/FAR printed). The panic reset path writes
"reset: ..." markers before PSCI SYSTEM_RESET, so a ring that ends without one was reset from outside (watchdog / hypervisor / PMIC).
kprintf lines (cpu_start(), arm_cpu_init() ... online) never reach ramoops; these events replace them. No effect with cpus=1
beyond cpu0's own cpu_machine_init / first-IPI lines. Needs package/RuanMacBootProgress.c from the same set.

